Dear Drug Safety Team,

I am writing to report an adverse drug reaction observed in one of my patients.

Patient: female, 62 years old, weight approx. 68 kg, history of hypertension and type 2 diabetes.
The patient was started on Cardiozin (generic name amlopril) 10mg once daily, oral, on 15-Jul-2026 for
blood pressure management. On 22-Jul-2026, seven days after starting the medication, she developed
severe swelling of the face and lips (angioedema) along with difficulty breathing. She was brought to our
clinic emergency room and required hospitalization for 2 days for observation and IV antihistamines/steroids.
She has since recovered fully and the drug was discontinued on 22-Jul-2026.

